<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>False</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<Title>YANLib</Title>
		<Authors>Yami An</Authors>
		<Company>YAN</Company>
		<Description>
			YANLib (YAMI AN NEPHILIM LIBRARY) is a comprehensive .NET utility library providing powerful extension methods that enhance developer productivity. Built on .NET 8 (LTS), it offers high-performance utilities for JSON serialization, text manipulation, object validation, task coordination, mathematical operations, DateTime handling, and more.

			Key features:
			• YANJson: High-performance JSON serialization with robust error handling
			• YANText: String manipulation, validation, and transformation with null safety
			• YANObject: Object validation, property analysis, and deep copying
			• YANTask: Enhanced task coordination with conditional waiting and error handling
			• YANUnmanaged: Type parsing and conversion with built-in error handling
			• YANRandom: Random value generation for various types and collections
			• YANMath: Mathematical operations with null handling and type conversion
			• YANDateTime: Time zone conversion and date calculations
			• YANProcess: Process management utilities
			• YANExpression: Dynamic property access and expression tree utilities

			All components feature fluent APIs, robust null handling, collection support, and performance optimizations. YANLib simplifies common programming tasks while maintaining high performance, making it an essential toolkit for .NET developers.
		</Description>
		<Copyright>Copyright ©  2023</Copyright>
		<PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Tynab/YANLib</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Tynab/YANLib</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageTags>C# .NET Library</PackageTags>
		<PackAsTool>False</PackAsTool>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>### YANLib 8.4.0 – Correctness, Performance and New Overloads

* **New API**: `ParseWith`/`ParsesWith` (parse with an `IFormatProvider`), `GenerateRandom&lt;T&gt;(T min, T max)` and `Random.NextChar(char min, char max)`, public `YANTask.WaitAnyWithConditions`/`WhenAnyWithConditions`, `YANProcess` overloads with `entireProcessTree` and `CancellationToken`, and `IsNull`/`IsNotNull` restored as obsolete shims.
* **Fixes**: `Parse` no longer crashes on out-of-range values and supports `nint`/`nuint`; exact integer/decimal math in `YANMath`; uniform, half-open `YANRandom` ranges; inherited properties, safe graph walks and runtime-type `Copy` in `YANObject`; prompt cancellation and O(n) completion order in `YANTask`; robust `YANProcess` kills; `Snowflake` sequence, extraction and validation fixes; order-preserving collection helpers.
* **Faster**: TryParse instead of exceptions, no boxing in typed `Sum`/`Average`, compiled property accessors in `YANObject`.
* **Behaviour changes to check**: `IdGenerator.NextId*` throws for an epoch in the future or 2^41 ms or more in the past; `GenerateRandom&lt;T&gt;(a, b)` with two typed numeric, `DateTime` or `char` arguments returns a value in [a, b); inherited properties count in `IsNullDefault`; collection helpers are lazy and ordered.
* **Package**: ships XML docs, no `favicon.ico` content file, API validated against 8.3.3.

Full list: [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/Tynab/YANLib/blob/develop/CHANGELOG.md). Documentation: [https://github.com/Tynab/YANLib/wiki](https://github.com/Tynab/YANLib/wiki)</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>False</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
		<PackageId>Tynab.YANLib</PackageId>
		<Version>8.4.0</Version>
		<LangVersion>12</LangVersion>
		<ProduceReferenceAssembly>True</ProduceReferenceAssembly>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
		<IncludeBuildOutput>true</IncludeBuildOutput>
		<!--
			Pack fails if the public API is not compatible with the baseline package downloaded from nuget.org
			during restore. Validation runs after the package is created, so a failed pack still leaves the
			.nupkg in the output folder: pack into an empty folder and never push after a failed pack.
			Validation is incremental: after changing only the baseline version, delete obj/ so that it runs again.
		-->
		<EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
		<PackageValidationBaselineVersion>8.3.3</PackageValidationBaselineVersion>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\..\README.md">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Include="..\..\res\icon.png">
		  <Pack>True</Pack>
		  <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="YANLib.Tests" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<ProjectReference Include="..\YANLib.Implementation\YANLib.Implementation.csproj">
			<PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
		</ProjectReference>
	</ItemGroup>

	<!--
		YANLib.Implementation is not published as its own package (PrivateAssets="all"), so its assembly is
		shipped inside this package. Asking the referenced project for its output path keeps the packed file in
		sync with the build (it honours the configuration, OutputPath and an output directory given on the
		command line) and also works when packing an already built tree without building it again.
	-->
	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetsForTfmSpecificBuildOutput>$(TargetsForTfmSpecificBuildOutput);IncludeImplementationAssembly</TargetsForTfmSpecificBuildOutput>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<Target Name="IncludeImplementationAssembly">
		<MSBuild Projects="@(ProjectReference)" Condition="'%(ProjectReference.PrivateAssets)' == 'all'" Targets="GetTargetPath">
			<Output TaskParameter="TargetOutputs" ItemName="_YanPrivateReferenceAssembly" />
		</MSBuild>
		<ItemGroup>
			<BuildOutputInPackage Include="@(_YanPrivateReferenceAssembly)" />
		</ItemGroup>
	</Target>

</Project>
